{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RFEuA6u3MBUbj1YCYNk4Sr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"use client\";\n2\t\n3\timport { useEffect, useEffectEvent } from \"react\";\n4\timport { trackBeginCheckout } from \"@/lib/gtm-ecommerce\";\n5\t\n6\tconst CHECKOUT_ITEMS = [\n7\t  {\n8\t    item_id: \"standard-capsule-pod\",\n9\t    item_name: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n10\t    item_category: \"accommodation\",\n11\t    price: 35,\n12\t    currency: \"MYR\",\n13\t  },\n14\t];\n15\t\n16\texport default function BookEcommerceTracker() {\n17\t  // Initialize GA4 custom dimension for A/B test variant on mount\n18\t  useEffect(() => {\n19\t    if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return;\n20\t    const variant = document.cookie\n21\t      .split(\"; \")\n22\t      .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n23\t      ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n24\t\n25\t    // Set custom dimension for variant tracking in GA4\n26\t    const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n27\t    w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n28\t    w.dataLayer.push({\n29\t      event: \"page_view\",\n30\t      \"dimension_1\": variant, // dimension_1 = CTA variant (configure in GA4)\n31\t    });\n32\t  }, []);\n33\t\n34\t  const handleBookNowClick = useEffectEvent((e: MouseEvent) => {\n35\t    const target = e.target as HTMLElement;\n36\t    const link = target.closest(\"a[href*='wa.me'], a[href='#booking'], .btn-primary\");\n37\t    if (link) {\n38\t      // Include variant in ecommerce tracking\n39\t      const variant = document.cookie\n40\t        .split(\"; \")\n41\t        .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n42\t        ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n43\t\n44\t      trackBeginCheckout(CHECKOUT_ITEMS);\n45\t\n46\t      // Log CTA click with variant\n47\t      const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n48\t      w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n49\t      w.dataLayer.push({\n50\t        event: \"cta_click\",\n51\t        \"dimension_1\": variant,\n52\t      });\n53\t    }\n54\t  });\n55\t\n56\t  useEffect(() => {\n57\t    document.addEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n58\t    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n59\t  }, []);\n60\t\n61\t  return null;\n62\t}\n63\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d01e663f-72a6-4a53-a5eb-adc0e9c4425b","uuid":"92dbd744-f998-40b8-85fd-30e61f4f9b35","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:12:28.854Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\components\\BookEcommerceTracker.tsx","content":"\"use client\";\n\nimport { useEffect, useEffectEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { trackBeginCheckout } from \"@/lib/gtm-ecommerce\";\n\nconst CHECKOUT_ITEMS = [\n  {\n    item_id: \"standard-capsule-pod\",\n    item_name: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n    item_category: \"accommodation\",\n    price: 35,\n    currency: \"MYR\",\n  },\n];\n\nexport default function BookEcommerceTracker() {\n  // Initialize GA4 custom dimension for A/B test variant on mount\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return;\n    const variant = document.cookie\n      .split(\"; \")\n      .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n      ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n\n    // Set custom dimension for variant tracking in GA4\n    const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n    w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n    w.dataLayer.push({\n      event: \"page_view\",\n      \"dimension_1\": variant, // dimension_1 = CTA variant (configure in GA4)\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  const handleBookNowClick = useEffectEvent((e: MouseEvent) => {\n    const target = e.target as HTMLElement;\n    const link = target.closest(\"a[href*='wa.me'], a[href='#booking'], .btn-primary\");\n    if (link) {\n      // Include variant in ecommerce tracking\n      const variant = document.cookie\n        .split(\"; \")\n        .find((row) => row.startsWith(\"x-variant=\"))\n        ?.split(\"=\")[1] || \"book-now\";\n\n      trackBeginCheckout(CHECKOUT_ITEMS);\n\n      // Log CTA click with variant\n      const w = window as unknown as { dataLayer: Record<string, unknown>[] };\n      w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n      w.dataLayer.push({\n        event: \"cta_click\",\n        \"dimension_1\": variant,\n      });\n    }\n  });\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    document.addEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n    return () => document.removeEventListener(\"click\", handleBookNowClick);\n  }, []);\n\n  return null;\n}\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015PFrfNycVheqBkrYu8ZGr7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! So the implementation already has:\n\n1. ✓ `@vercel/edge-config` and `@vercel/flags` packages installed\n2. ✓ `flags.ts` with types and flag functions for CTA variant\n3. ✓ `middleware.ts` that evaluates the variant and sets x-variant cookie\n4. ✓ `/book/page.tsx` that reads the variant from the middleware header\n5. ✓ `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx` that reads the variant cookie and sends it to GA4 with dimension_1\n\nHowever, I need to check the acceptance criteria to see what's missing:\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n1. ✓ Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project (implied by packages)\n2. ✓ @vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\n3. ✓ A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (already defined in flags.ts and being used in page.tsx)\n4. ✓ Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\n5. ✓ GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis (in BookEcommerceTracker)\n6. ? Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\n\nThe issue is that the current implementation is using a mock/fallback system. According to the technical notes and acceptance criteria, we need to:\n1. Actually connect to Vercel Edge Config to read the flag\n2. Make sure the implementation is production-ready with Edge Config\n\nThe problem noted in the story is: \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\"\n\nThis suggests that the previous attempt might have included unnecessary changes or files. The current implementation seems to already have most of what's needed, but we need to:\n\n\nLooking at flags.ts more closely, I see it's currently using mock values with a comment about needing to import from @vercel/edge-config. The middleware and page components are set up correctly, but the actual flag evaluation needs to pull from Edge Config using the `get()` function rather than relying on fallback values. I should verify the environment variable setup for the Edge Config connection as well.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":83622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d01e663f-72a6-4a53-a5eb-adc0e9c4425b","uuid":"166548c1-81fa-4ecd-b7c9-6b64b1156cd2"}
