{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HBDF4a8Kg3Ez4hQFktTbqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. So the environment is set up but the implementation is still using mock flags. Looking at the story requirements again:\n\nThe issue is that the implementation is currently using mock flags instead of actually reading from Vercel Edge Config. According to the acceptance criteria, it should:\n\n1. \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware\" - ✓ already done\n2. \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received\" - ✓ already done\n3. \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status\" - This requires actual Edge Config connection\n\nThe key missing piece is updating `flags.ts` to actually use `@vercel/edge-config`'s `get()` function instead of just using mock values.\n\nAccording to the technical notes:\n```\nRead flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\n```\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Update `flags.ts` to import and use `@vercel/edge-config`'s `get()` function\n2. Keep fallback behavior for local development\n3. Ensure middleware is still working correctly\n\nLet me create a plan before making any changes:\n\n## Current State\n- Basic A/B testing infrastructure is in place (flags.ts, middleware.ts, page.tsx, BookEcommerceTracker.tsx)\n- Packages (@vercel/edge-config, @vercel/flags) are installed\n- Implementation uses mock flags instead of reading from Vercel Edge Config\n\n## Problem Identified\n- `flags.ts` is not actually reading from Vercel Edge Config - it's using mock values from environment variables\n- The implementation needs to use `@vercel/edge-config`'s `get()` function for production\n- Acceptance criteria #6 (Vercel Flags UI in dashboard) requires actual Edge Config connection\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Update `flags.ts` to import `get` from `@vercel/edge-config`\n\n\n- Modify the `getFlag()` function to attempt reading from Edge Config with a fallback to environment variables and defaults for local development\n- Confirm middleware.ts continues functioning as expected\n- Ensure page.tsx and BookEcommerceTracker.tsx require no modifications\n- Validate the setup works locally with fallbacks and is prepared for production Edge Config integration\n\nThis should be a minimal change to the existing code - just updating the flag reading logic.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d01e663f-72a6-4a53-a5eb-adc0e9c4425b","uuid":"0d78ef6f-99a2-4bef-97d6-ab17dc15b1b2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HBDF4a8Kg3Ez4hQFktTbqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\n\nThe project already has:\n- `@vercel/edge-config` and `@vercel/flags` packages installed\n- `flags.ts` with CTA variant types and mock flag logic\n- `middleware.ts` evaluating variant and setting x-variant cookie\n- `/book/page.tsx` using variant from middleware header\n- `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx` tracking variant in GA4 dimension_1\n\n**However**, `flags.ts` is currently using **mock values** instead of reading from Vercel Edge Config. The implementation needs to use `@vercel/edge-config`'s `get()` function.\n\n## Problem Identified\n\nThe acceptance criteria requires \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware\" with \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard.\" The current implementation won't work with the Vercel dashboard because it's not actually reading from Edge Config—it's using environment variable mocks.\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n- Update `flags.ts` to import `get` from `@vercel/edge-config` and call it in `getFlag()`\n- Keep fallback to environment/defaults for local development\n- Verify middleware, page, and tracker components still work\n- Minimal changes to minimize diff size (current story marked as oversized at 12854 lines)\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/lib/flags.ts\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 30\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow executing the implementation:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d01e663f-72a6-4a53-a5eb-adc0e9c4425b","uuid":"672ae28e-acb4-4123-a4a5-3010dc82b9b4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HBDF4a8Kg3Ez4hQFktTbqJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QqVa71d3Ba1f7gzpQVFQTR","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\lib\\flags.ts","old_string":"/**\n * Vercel Feature Flags and flag resolution logic.\n * Defines flag types and server-side flag reading from Edge Config.\n * For local dev, falls back to mock flags from environment variables.\n */\n\nexport type CTAVariant = \"book-now\" | \"check-availability\" | \"best-price-direct\";\n\nexport interface FlagsConfig {\n  \"cta-variant\": CTAVariant;\n}\n\n// Default flags for local development / fallback\nconst DEFAULT_FLAGS: FlagsConfig = {\n  \"cta-variant\": \"book-now\",\n};\n\n// Mock flag values from environment\nconst MOCK_FLAGS: Partial<FlagsConfig> = {\n  \"cta-variant\":\n    (process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT as CTAVariant) ?? \"book-now\",\n};\n\n/**\n * Get a flag value from Edge Config (production) or mock (local dev).\n * In production, reads from Vercel Edge Config.\n * In development, uses mock values from environment variables.\n *\n * @param key - The flag key (e.g., 'cta-variant')\n * @param defaultValue - Fallback value if flag is not found\n * @returns The flag value\n */\nexport async function getFlag<K extends keyof FlagsConfig>(\n  key: K,\n  defaultValue?: FlagsConfig[K]\n): Promise<FlagsConfig[K]> {\n  try {\n    // In production with Vercel Edge Config, import and use @vercel/edge-config\n    // For now, use mock values that respect environment overrides\n    const mockValue = MOCK_FLAGS[key];\n    if (mockValue !== undefined) {\n      return mockValue as FlagsConfig[K];\n    }\n\n    // Fall back to defaults\n    return defaultValue ?? DEFAULT_FLAGS[key];\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`[flags] Error reading flag '${key}':`, error);\n    return defaultValue ?? DEFAULT_FLAGS[key];\n  }\n}","new_string":"/**\n * Vercel Feature Flags and flag resolution logic.\n * Defines flag types and server-side flag reading from Edge Config.\n * For local dev, falls back to mock flags from environment variables.\n */\n\nimport { get } from \"@vercel/edge-config\";\n\nexport type CTAVariant = \"book-now\" | \"check-availability\" | \"best-price-direct\";\n\nexport interface FlagsConfig {\n  \"cta-variant\": CTAVariant;\n}\n\n// Default flags for local development / fallback\nconst DEFAULT_FLAGS: FlagsConfig = {\n  \"cta-variant\": \"book-now\",\n};\n\n// Mock flag values from environment (for local dev when Edge Config is unavailable)\nconst MOCK_FLAGS: Partial<FlagsConfig> = {\n  \"cta-variant\":\n    (process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT as CTAVariant) ?? \"book-now\",\n};\n\n/**\n * Get a flag value from Vercel Edge Config (production) or fallback to mock/defaults (local dev).\n * In production on Vercel, reads from Edge Config (reads < 1ms p99 globally).\n * In development, uses mock values from environment variables, then defaults.\n *\n * @param key - The flag key (e.g., 'cta-variant')\n * @param defaultValue - Fallback value if flag is not found\n * @returns The flag value\n */\nexport async function getFlag<K extends keyof FlagsConfig>(\n  key: K,\n  defaultValue?: FlagsConfig[K]\n): Promise<FlagsConfig[K]> {\n  try {\n    // Try reading from Vercel Edge Config first (production)\n    const edgeConfigValue = await get<FlagsConfig[K]>(key);\n    if (edgeConfigValue !== undefined) {\n      return edgeConfigValue;\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    // Edge Config is not available (local dev, not on Vercel, etc.)\n    // Fall through to mock/default values\n  }\n\n  // Fall back to mock values from environment\n  const mockValue = MOCK_FLAGS[key];\n  if (mockValue !== undefined) {\n    return mockValue as FlagsConfig[K];\n  }\n\n  // Ultimate fallback to defaults\n  return defaultValue ?? DEFAULT_FLAGS[key];\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d01e663f-72a6-4a53-a5eb-adc0e9c4425b","uuid":"834985b8-e9cc-4cab-83e0-8dd1611ae4ca"}
